Example System: AX = b
 

\begin{cases}
x + 2y + z = 2 \\
3x + 8y + z = 12 \\
4y + z = 2
\end{cases}

 
Augmented matrix (extra column for b):
 

\left[
\begin{array}{ccc|c}
1 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\
3 & 8 & 1 & 12 \\
0 & 4 & 1 & 2
\end{array}
\right]

 
First pivot: A_{11} = 1
 
Elimination step (2,1):
 

\left[
\begin{array}{ccc|c}
1 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\
0 & 2 & -2 & 6 \\
0 & 4 & 1 & 2
\end{array}
\right]

 
Step (3,2):
 

\left[
\begin{array}{ccc|c}
1 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\
0 & 2 & -2 & 6 \\
0 & 0 & 5 & -10
\end{array}
\right]

 
Upper triangular matrix U and c:
 

U = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 1 \\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\ 0 & 0 & 5 \end{bmatrix}, \quad c = \begin{bmatrix} 2 \\ 6 \\ -10 \end{bmatrix}

 
Back-substitution:
 
- 5z = -10 \implies z = -2
- 2y - 2z = 6 \implies y = 1
- x + 2y + z = 2 \implies x = 2
 
Solution: x=2,\ y=1,\ z=-2
 
 
 
Elimination Matrices
 
Step 1: subtract 3 \times \text{row 1} from row 2
 

E_{21} = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix}

 

E_{21}A = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 1 \\ 3 & 8 & 1 \\ 0 & 4 & 1 \end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 1 \\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\ 0 & 4 & 1 \end{bmatrix}

 
Step 2: subtract 2 \times \text{row 2} from row 3
 

E_{32} = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\ 0 & -2 & 1 \end{bmatrix}

 

E_{32}(E_{21}A) = U \quad \Rightarrow \quad (E_{32}E_{21})A = U

 

E_{32}
\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 1 \\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\ 0 & 4 & 1 \end{bmatrix}
= \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 1 \\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\ 0 & 0 & 5 \end{bmatrix}

 
 
 
Matrix Multiplication Notes
 
Matrix × column = column:
 

\begin{bmatrix} - & - & - \\ - & - & - \\ - & - & - \end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix} 3 \\ 4 \\ 5 \end{bmatrix}
= 3 \times \text{col1} + 4 \times \text{col2} + 5 \times \text{col3}

 
Row × matrix = row:
 

\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 7 \end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix} - & - & - \\ - & - & - \\ - & - & - \end{bmatrix}
= 1 \times \text{row1} + 2 \times \text{row2} + 7 \times \text{row3}

